WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.197 --> 00:00:01.030
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.110
- [Narrator] Welcome to Lima,

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.870
the only Latin American
capital facing the ocean,

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.620
a culinary North Star in South America.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.720
The cuisine draws influence
from both the land and the sea.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.033
And we're here to explore,
of course, the street food.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.730
In the neighborhood of
Surquillo you'll find

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.300
a one-man band cooking some
of the best seafood in town,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.083
it's a dish with a serious kick.

00:00:27.724 --> 00:00:30.474
(exciting music)

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.487
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.800
Head toward the neighborhood
of La Punta in Callao

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.360
and meet Juan Hernandez,

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.413
a fishmonger turned
sandwich-maker-extraordinaire.

00:01:37.242 --> 00:01:41.159
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.990
Back in Surquillo we're at
the stand of Mrs. Chinén

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:33.163
who makes a Peruvian classic
you cannot afford to miss.

00:02:36.582 --> 00:02:40.499
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.670
For those with a sweet
tooth we head to eat

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:36.663
a dessert made from corn, purple corn.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:44.703
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:04:30.285 --> 00:04:33.410
Finally, we're in the traditional
neighborhood of Magdalena,

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.340
at a hidden stand serving a dish

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.690
that might might you
rethink the humble potato.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:45.284
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:05:40.186 --> 00:05:42.353
(chiming)

